librevenge changes for nitrocdr (scripts/get-deps.sh applies this after downloading):
- RVNGProperty::getBinaryData(): the data of a binary property (embedded images) without
  converting it to base64 and back
- property lists are moved, not deep-copied: RVNGPropertyList / RVNGPropertyListVector move
  constructors, RVNGPropertyListVector::append(RVNGPropertyList &&), at() and
  RVNGPropertyList::insert(name, RVNGPropertyListVector &&); inserting a property no longer
  clones it once more on its way into the map (RVNGPropertyListElement is moved);
  LIBREVENGE_PROPERTYLIST_MOVE tells the libcdr fork it can use these
- RVNGPropertyList::insert(name, string) tries the number / unit parsers (slow: boost::spirit
  rebuilding its tables) only for strings that can start a number
Together with the libcdr fork's use of them, a big ArchiCAD plan (17 MB CDR) loads 2.7 x faster.
And a fix:
- RVNGOLEStream: a damaged header's block size exponent clamped to 30, not 31 (compute_block_size
  asserts it is below 31: the viewer aborted on such a file; valid() refuses it anyway)

